    w: 1, title: "Why Study Prophecy? Introduction to Responsible Reading", theme: "Prophecy is a gift that strengthens faith, calls to holiness and gives hope, and it must be read carefully, humbly and in context, avoiding speculation, sensationalism and date-setting",
    summary: "This opening lesson introduces the course. Revelation 1:3 blesses those who read, hear and keep the words of this prophecy. Second Peter 1:19-21 says prophecy came from men moved by the Holy Spirit and should not be a matter of one's own interpretation. Deuteronomy 18:21-22 gives a test of true prophecy. The lesson explains why we study prophecy, the dangers of misuse, the principles of responsible reading, and the course plan, and notes that Christians differ on many details.",
